{
  "_comment": "Clean-room SA-02m template for the Saifuli MTDX62-MB presence sensor. MTD262-MB (24 GHz) and MTD062-MB (5.8 GHz) share this map. Register numbers are the public Modbus map (holding 0..6 tuning, holding 7..9 identity, input 0..3 measurements). This file is not a Wiren Board template. Holding 7 is the slave id, holding 8 the baud, holding 9 the parity — those are not channels, writing them drops the sensor off the bus. The scan recognizes that triple plus input 0 (presence 0/1) and input 3 (status 0..6). On a port that already has devices the sensor uses that port's baud and 8N1. stopbits 2 is only for a sensor that answers the 8N2 pass and nothing else.",
  "device": {
